  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is an Array?</h2>
    <p><b>Array = A List.</b> One variable that stores many values together in order.</p>
    <p>Example: You have 100 students. Without an array, you need 100 variables - student1, student2, student3... With an array, you need only 1 variable - <code>students</code>.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Real Life Example:</b> A shopping list, a class attendance list, a playlist of songs. All of these are arrays - a list of items in one place.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Shopping List</h2>
    <p>Add items, remove items. This is an array:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <h3 style="margin:0">🛒 My Shopping List</h3>
      <p id="demoList" style="margin:12px 0">Loading list...</p>
      <p style="color:#64748b">Total Items: <b id="demoCount">0</b></p>
      <input class="demo-input" id="itemInput" type="text" placeholder="Type item - e.g. Milk">
      <button class="btn btn-js" onclick="addItem()">Add Item ➕</button>
      <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="removeItem()">Remove Last ➖</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="resetDemo()">Reset ↺</button>
    </div>
    <h2>3. How to Create an Array?</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let fruits = ["Apple", "Banana", "Mango"];</span><br>
<span class="text">let marks = [85, 90, 78, 92];</span><br>
<span class="text">let mixed = ["Ali", 20, true]; // Array can hold different types</span><br>
<span class="text">let empty = []; // Empty array</span>
    </code></div>
    <p>Array uses <b>square brackets [ ]</b>. Values are separated by <b>comma ,</b>.</p>
    <h2>4. Index - Position Number</h2>
    <p>Every item in an array has a position number called <b>Index</b>. Index always starts from <b>0</b>, not 1.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Index</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Value</td><td>"Apple"</td><td>"Banana"</td><td>"Mango"</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let fruits = ["Apple", "Banana", "Mango"];</span><br><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits[0]); // "Apple" - First item</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits[1]); // "Banana"</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits[2]); // "Mango" - Last item</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits[3]); // undefined - No item at 3</span><br><br>
<span class="text">fruits[1] = "Orange"; // Change Banana to Orange</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits); // ["Apple", "Orange", "Mango"]</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Biggest Beginner Mistake:</b> People think first item is at index 1. It is at index 0. So last item is always at <code>length - 1</code>.</div>
    <h2>5. length - How Many Items?</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let fruits = ["Apple", "Banana", "Mango"];</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits.length); // 3</span><br><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits[fruits.length - 1]); // "Mango" - Last item trick</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Array Methods - Add / Remove</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Method</th><th>What It Does</th><th>Example</th><th>Result</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>push()</b></td><td>Add at END</td><td>fruits.push("Grapes")</td><td>["Apple","Banana","Mango","Grapes"]</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>pop()</b></td><td>Remove from END</td><td>fruits.pop()</td><td>Removes "Grapes"</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>unshift()</b></td><td>Add at START</td><td>fruits.unshift("Kiwi")</td><td>["Kiwi","Apple",...]</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>shift()</b></td><td>Remove from START</td><td>fruits.shift()</td><td>Removes "Kiwi"</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>includes()</b></td><td>Check if exists?</td><td>fruits.includes("Apple")</td><td>true / false</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>indexOf()</b></td><td>Find position</td><td>fruits.indexOf("Mango")</td><td>2</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let fruits = ["Apple", "Banana"];</span><br>
<span class="text">fruits.push("Mango"); // ["Apple", "Banana", "Mango"]</span><br>
<span class="text">fruits.pop(); // ["Apple", "Banana"] - Mango removed</span><br>
<span class="text">fruits.unshift("Kiwi"); // ["Kiwi", "Apple", "Banana"]</span><br>
<span class="text">fruits.shift(); // ["Apple", "Banana"] - Kiwi removed</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Loop Through Array - Show All Items</h2>
    <p>Loop + Array are best friends. Loop runs through all items one by one.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let fruits = ["Apple", "Banana", "Mango"];</span><br><br>
<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < fruits.length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log(i + " - " + fruits[i]);</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Output: 0 - Apple, 1 - Banana, 2 - Mango</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Remember:</b> Loop starts from <code>i = 0</code> for arrays, because index starts from 0. Loop runs while <code>i &lt; length</code>, not <code>i &lt;= length</code>.</p>
    <h2>8. Complete Example - Student List</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"list"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Students</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"name"</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"text"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Student Name"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"addStudent()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Add Student</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let students = ["Ali", "Sara"];</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function showStudents() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let html = "";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < students.length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">html = html + (i + 1) + ". " + students[i] + "&lt;br&gt;";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("list").innerHTML = html;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function addStudent() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let n = document.getElementById("name").value;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (n !== "") { students.push(n); showStudents(); }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">showStudents(); // Show on page load</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>9. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. Array <code>let prices = [100, 200, 300]</code> - Use loop to show total of all prices<br>2. Array of 5 friends names - Use loop to show all names on page<br>3. Shopping list like demo - Input + Add button with push(), Remove button with pop()</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Array = List in [ ] | Index starts from 0 | length = How many items | Last item = array[length - 1] | push() = Add at end | pop() = Remove from end | unshift() = Add at start | shift() = Remove from start | Loop for array: for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++)</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson28">Lesson 28 - Objects</a> - Learn how to store one person with name, age, city together. Array is a list, Object is a profile.</p>
